course: dictionary
lesson: 10768
title: Context clues: a dinosaur name
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are hard, even for clever readers. «Utahraptor» is one of them, but the words around it give you clues. «Utahraptor was about 6 metres long and as heavy as a polar bear, and lived earlier than Velociraptor.» The sentence tells you it is a dinosaur, because it lived long ago, and that it is huge.
explain: The sentence also says «most raptors were small». Raptor is the group that Utahraptor belongs to, and most of its relatives were small, so Utahraptor stands out for being big. Ask yourself: what kind of thing would fit here? Then test your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of the hard word.
explain: The first part of the name, Utah, is a clue to where it lived. Its dictionary meaning says it lived about 125 million years ago in what is now Utah, USA. When you are not sure, check a dictionary to confirm your guess.
fact: Utahraptor is a large meat-eating dinosaur with a big curved claw on each foot.
fact: Utahraptor lived about 125 million years ago.
fact: Utahraptor was about 6 to 7 metres long, much bigger than the real velociraptor.
fact: Fossils show that Utahraptor was related to birds and probably had feathers.
exercise: «Utahraptor was about 6 metres long.» How long was Utahraptor? | About 60 metres | About 60 centimetres | *About 6 metres | About 6 millimetres
exercise: Utahraptor lived in what is now Utah, USA. Where did it live? | Antarctica | Scotland | *Utah, USA | Australia
exercise: «Most raptors were small.» What does this tell you about Utahraptor? | *It was bigger than most raptors | It was a plant | It was smaller than most raptors | It had no claws
test: What feature did Utahraptor have on each foot? | A shell | A horn on its nose | A pair of wings | *A big curved claw
test: Fossils suggest Utahraptor was related to which kind of animal? | *Birds | Frogs | Snakes | Fish
exam: What do the clues «as heavy as a polar bear» and «most raptors were small» tell you about Utahraptor? | It was a plant that grew in Utah | *It was a big, heavy dinosaur, far bigger than most raptors | It lived in the sea and ate fish | It was small and light, like a sparrow
